{{! cas-replace-composite-property: sketch section 4.3's CompositePropertyBoundary CAS,
    dal:RowLevelGuardOnly variant.
    The aggregate is the root and every member in the family's data graph.
    The ownedPath slot is one SPARQL property path, compiled at compile time from
    the owned edges of the target's boundary shape (persistence.boundary,
    persistence.paths), so a recursion is a star, an edge from child to
    parent is an inverse step, and the path has no depth bound. A path
    cannot be a variable, and SPARQL permits one only inside WHERE, so ?s
    ranges over the root and each member there and the DELETE template
    consumes it. The path can match no steps, so ?s starts at the root. Every
    triple of the root and of each member is matched once, which is linear in
    the aggregate's size.
    Every pattern and the payload sit in the graph the dataGraph slot names, the profile's
    dal:dataGraph, and the default graph is never read or written (static
    check S-1). Only the receipt records go to the log graph. The version
    row's subject is the root instance IRI, never a graph IRI (sketch
    section 4.3).
    requestDigest is computed by the caller as lower-case
    hex SHA-256 over the tuple-encoded operation kind, target, expected
    seq and sorted canonical N-Triples of the skolemized payload (guide
    §15.2), and recorded on the txn claim so a confirmation can tell a
    replay from a different request reusing the txn id.
    payloadTriples is a request-time Mustache slot, not a
    SPARQL variable: a set of triples cannot be bound through one variable.
    Instantiate leaves it in place, and the caller renders it with the
    already-serialised, trusted payload triples before submission (see
    tools/persistence/README.md, "Using the generated SPARQL directly").
    Note for template authors: never put a Mustache tag inside this
    comment block. Chevron's comment parser ends at the first closing
    double-brace it sees, which silently truncates the comment. }}
PREFIX pat: <https://example.org/lattice/patterns#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

DELETE {
  GRAPH {{{dataGraph}}} { ?s ?p ?o }
  GRAPH {{{metaGraphPrefix}}} { $root pat:seq $expectedSeq ; pat:head ?prevRev }
}
INSERT {
  GRAPH {{{dataGraph}}} { {{{payloadTriples}}} }
  GRAPH {{{metaGraphPrefix}}} { $root pat:epoch $epoch ; pat:seq $nextSeq ; pat:head $newRev }
  GRAPH {{{txnGraph}}}        { $txnId pat:rev $newRev ; pat:requestDigest $requestDigest }
  GRAPH ?logGraph2 {
      $newRev a pat:Revision ; pat:target $root ; pat:epoch $epoch ; pat:seq $nextSeq ;
              pat:prevRev ?prevRev ; pat:txn ?txnKey ; pat:recordedAt ?now
  }
}
WHERE {
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR({{{logGraphPrefix}}}), SUBSTR(STR(NOW()), 1, 7))) AS ?logGraph)
  BIND(?logGraph AS ?logGraph2)
  GRAPH {{{metaGraphPrefix}}} {
      $root pat:epoch $epoch ; pat:seq $expectedSeq .
      OPTIONAL { $root pat:head ?prevRev }
      FILTER NOT EXISTS { $root pat:deleted true }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { GRAPH {{{txnGraph}}} { $txnId pat:rev ?any } }
  BIND(STR($txnId) AS ?txnKey)
  BIND(NOW() AS ?now)
  OPTIONAL { GRAPH {{{dataGraph}}} { $root {{{ownedPath}}} ?s . ?s ?p ?o } }
}
